    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0481" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control Austria/7–345: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 280<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy
                    </hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-03T15:00:00+02:00">July 3, 1945—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2850. Our 2842, July 2.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d280-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>June 30 [A]FHQ directed Brit Eight Army to contact local Russ Commander Sov
                    Forces in Styria to arrange for Sov withdrawal and subsequent Brit movement into
                    Styria and Carinthia areas of Austria.</p>
                <p>July 1 Brit officer commanding Fifth Corps met Russians at Sov Fourth Army HQ delivered letter from CG Eight Army addressed to Tolbukhin and discussed withdrawal Russ forces from Styria. Russ
                    Commander said he had not reed any orders to withdraw and until such time he
                    would maintain his position. USS[R] Com also asked what Brit intended to do with
                    White Russ Corps now in Brit occupied zone to which Brit officer replied he had
                    no knowledge of its existence. July 2 Brit officer CG Five Corps again met Russ and reed written reply addressed to
                        CG Eight Army saying latter’s letter would be
                    delivered promptly to Sov CinC Central Army
                    group Marshal Koniev; that until receipt
                    orders from CinC Russ Forces in Styria could
                    not be withdrawn. Note was cordial in tone.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
